[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990188229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990188229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990188229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yOqbF","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T08:00:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T08:01:03Z","body":"I don't think this is a good idea. This PR automatically adjusts the layout padding, which effectively disables `edge-to-edge` mode for all Godot apps.\r\n\r\nWhile it might make sense to disable `edge-to-edge` for the Android editor but for exported projects, we should leave this decision to the users. Godot already provides methods like [get_display_safe_area()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-safe-area) and [get_display_cutouts()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-cutouts), which can be used to handle edge-to-edge layout properly.\r\n\r\nAlso, Android 15 deprecates the ability to change system bar colors programmatically. So, if we go ahead with this change, every non-immersive Godot app would end up with black bars on the top and bottom, which would clash with the app theme.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I would prefer keeping my app in edge-to-edge mode, rendering the background across the full screen, and placing the main content within the safe area using `DisplayServer.get_display_safe_area()`. This way, the system bars remain colored and match the app theme.\r\n\r\nThere's already ways for users to workaround this new restriction without disabling the `edge-to-edge` mode entirely.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990188229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990335164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990335164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990335164,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPOS8","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T08:54:51Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T08:54:51Z","body":"> I don't think this is a good idea. This PR automatically adjusts the layout padding, which effectively disables `edge-to-edge` mode for all Godot apps.\n> \n> While it might make sense to disable `edge-to-edge` for the Android editor but for exported projects, we should leave this decision to the users. Godot already provides methods like [get_display_safe_area()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-safe-area) and [get_display_cutouts()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-cutouts), which can be used to handle edge-to-edge layout properly.\n> \n\nThis PR maintains the current behavior prior to the bump to target SDK 35, which is that we only allow the app to be either immersive (system bars auto dismiss) or not edge-to-edge (system bars show and the content don't overlap them); you can test with a 4.4 build and validate that it's the case.\n\nSupporting edge-to-edge would be a new feature and that's not the role of this PR. Also given that we're in feature freeze, that would be something to discuss for 4.6 if we want to consider it.\n\n> Also, Android 15 deprecates the ability to change system bar colors programmatically. So, if we go ahead with this change, every non-immersive Godot app would end up with black bars on the top and bottom, which would clash with the app theme.\n> \n\nThe PR uses `enableEdgeToEdge()` which is recommended by Google to make the system bars transparent, so we're following the guideline.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990335164/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990404959","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990404959","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990404959,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPfVf","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:12:36Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:12:36Z","body":"In short the primary requirement for this PR should be `does it maintain the existing behavior as in 4.4 when exporting to Android`.\n\nThat's all this PR should be tested against, because for most users not paying close attention to Android changes, a change in layout behavior from one version of Godot to the next, in the same project is a breaking change.\n\nOnce we validate we are maintaining the existing (expected) behavior, we can then discuss how to surface the new edge-to-edge functionality in a way that's easy to integrate. \nThat'll be a new feature (so likely 4.6) and that'll be off by default, so users that don't want the feature don't have to deal with it.\n For a proper integration, we'll also need to update the documentation and provide tutorials for how to enable it and use the existing APIs to figure where to safely draw content.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990404959/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990407183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990407183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990407183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPf4P","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:13:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:13:09Z","body":"> > I don't think this is a good idea. This PR automatically adjusts the layout padding, which effectively disables `edge-to-edge` mode for all Godot apps.\r\n> > While it might make sense to disable `edge-to-edge` for the Android editor but for exported projects, we should leave this decision to the users. Godot already provides methods like [get_display_safe_area()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-safe-area) and [get_display_cutouts()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-get-display-cutouts), which can be used to handle edge-to-edge layout properly.\r\n> \r\n> This PR maintains the current behavior prior to the bump to target SDK 35, which is that we only allow the app to be either immersive (system bars auto dismiss) or not edge-to-edge (system bars show and the content don't overlap them); you can test with a 4.4 build and validate that it's the case.\r\n\r\nYeah, This PR does maintain the behaviour prior to the bump. However, `edge-to-edge` was achivable using a plugin but that won't be possible after this PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990407183/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990442881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990442881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990442881,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPomB","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:21:55Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:21:55Z","body":"> Yeah, This PR does maintain the behaviour prior to the bump. However, edge-to-edge was achivable using a plugin but that won't be possible after this PR.\n\nWell it sounds that in either case the plugin is obsolete:\n- without this change, apps are edge-to-edge by default, so there's no longer a need for the plugin\n- with this change, we'll add the edge-to-edge capability in Godot 4.6 in the engine, so the plugin will be obsolete then \n\nThe only issue is that the capability may be lost in Godot 4.5.. If we think that's an issue, then adding an export option to enable edge-to-edge should be trivial; but that means updating the documentation and providing tutorials for 4.5.. if you're up for it, it's worth considering..","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990442881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990460033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990460033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990460033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPsyB","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:25:45Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:26:01Z","body":"> without this change, apps are edge-to-edge by default, so there's no longer a need for the plugin\r\n\r\nThis is only the case for Android 15+ devices. Without this PR, plugin would work as expected on older devices.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990460033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990494401","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990494401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990494401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yP1LB","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:33:59Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:53:57Z","body":"> The only issue is that the capability may be lost in Godot 4.5.. If we think that's an issue, then adding an export option to enable edge-to-edge should be trivial; but that means updating the documentation and providing tutorials for 4.5.. if you're up for it, it's worth considering..\r\n\r\nYeah, that's my concern, the capability would be lost in 4.5. Okay, Let's go with this PR for now. I'll send one to enable `edge-to-edge`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990494401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990850805","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2990850805","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2990850805,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yRML1","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T10:30:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T10:30:21Z","body":"> > The only issue is that the capability may be lost in Godot 4.5.. If we think that's an issue, then adding an export option to enable edge-to-edge should be trivial; but that means updating the documentation and providing tutorials for 4.5.. if you're up for it, it's worth considering..\r\n> \r\n> Yeah, that's my concern, the capability would be lost in 4.5. Okay, Let's go with this PR for now. I'll send one to enable `edge-to-edge`.\r\n\r\n@syntaxerror247 I've updated the PR and included an export option for `edge-to-edge`. Can you take another look.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990850805/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993900696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2993900696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2993900696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yc0yY","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T03:03:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T07:42:28Z","body":"> * mention in the documentation that `edge_to_edge` does not support every device\r\n\r\nI think, edge-to-edge should be supported for every SDK 24+ device. I haven't tested though. \r\n\r\n> * Is it possible to change `edge_to_edge` at runtime?\r\n\r\nNot yet! Let's not block this PR, I'll send one to change it at runtime using WINDOW_MODE_MAXIMIZED (for Godot 4.6).\r\nIdeally, WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN should be for `immersive` and WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN for `edge-to-edge` but currently both are used for immersive and changing that would break compatibility.\r\n\r\n> * In the `Window Management` demo, I was also able to change `Immersive Mode` at runtime. Perhaps the export settings could be removed(?) if it works at runtime and can be changed via the project settings.\r\n\r\nWe are keeping the export option to instantly apply the immersive/edge-to-edge mode on launch otherwise it would create a slight noticable delay. ProjectSettings are initialised a bit late in the process.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993900696/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994099745","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#issuecomment-2994099745","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","id":2994099745,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ydlYh","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T10:11:17Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T10:11:17Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994099745/reactions","total_count":